{
  "about": "S-auth - the states of /login and /register the two frames do not draw (PLAN 4.1 rule 7), and the typed values of auth-2. Every state is signed out (account null) and replay: the only GETs are /config and the declared 401 on /auth/me. No form is ever submitted to the server: every submit outcome is a mutation-outcome fixture (a status and the error envelope of backend/src/lib/http.js sendError), answered in the browser, so no login or registration budget is spent and no account is created. The busy state (a request in flight) cannot be held by the capture tool and is reported as structure.",
  "overrides": {
    "auth-2": {
      "why": "auth-2 draws the register form filled: takacs.daniel@pelda.hu with the format tick and 14 masked characters. The values are typed by the capture (no request is sent). A last click on the wordmark takes the focus off the password field, as the frame draws both fields at rest.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "type": {
            "role": "textbox",
            "name": {
              "key": "auth.email"
            },
            "text": "takacs.daniel@pelda.hu"
          },
          "arrived": {
            "role": "textbox",
            "name": {
              "key": "auth.email"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": {
            "role": "textbox",
            "name": {
              "key": "auth.password"
            },
            "text": "Pulse-sample-1"
          },
          "arrived": {
            "role": "button",
            "name": {
              "key": "auth.showPassword"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "click": {
            "role": "heading",
            "name": {
              "re": "^tracker$"
            }
          },
          "arrived": {
            "role": "button",
            "name": {
              "key": "auth.showPassword"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
